---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { CoffeeCup, Gift, Mail, SendMail } from 'iconoir-react';
import yayImg from '../../assets/images/mailing-list-yay.png';
import Quote from '../shared/Quote.astro';
import LinkButton from '../shared/LinkButton.astro';
---

<div class="space-y-3 md:space-y-3">
	<div class="space-y-3 md:space-y-3">
		<h2
			transition:name="page-title"
			class="rounded-xl py-3 text-center font-serif text-lg font-bold xl:text-3xl"
		>
			<Mail className="inline pr-4 text-2xl text-amber-600 xl:text-4xl" />
			The Occasional Email Experience
		</h2>

		<div class="relative top-3 clear-left flex flex-col md:flex-row">
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-3">
				<Image alt="hooray" src={yayImg} />
				<p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs italic">
					the joy of receiving an email from Neil Hughes cannot be contained in
					a mere picture, but this comes close
				</p>
			</div>
			<div
				class="mr-12 mb-6 space-y-3 rounded bg-amber-100 px-12 py-6 md:space-y-6"
			>
				<p
					class="text-lg first-letter:float-left first-letter:pr-2 first-letter:text-5xl first-line:small-caps xl:text-2xl xl:first-letter:text-6xl"
				>
					Most emails are terrible. So I aim to make my emails a <strong
						class="text-red-500">special occasion</strong
					>.
				</p>
				<p>
					<SendMail
						className="inline pr-4 text-2xl text-zinc-500 xl:text-3xl"
					/> Sign up below and I&apos;ll send you <span
						class="font-bold text-green-600"
						>funny stories which may mildly improve your life</span
					>.
				</p>
				<p>
					<CoffeeCup
						className="inline pr-4 text-2xl text-zinc-500 xl:text-3xl"
					/>
					When a rare email arrives, grab a cup of tea and settle in to enjoy.
				</p>
				<p class="leading-loose">
					<Gift className="inline pr-4 text-2xl text-zinc-500 xl:text-3xl" />In
					your welcome email, I'll include the opening chapters of my books, <a
						href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}books/walking-on-custard`}
						class="text-blue-500 underline hover:text-blue-400"
					>
						Walking on Custard
					</a>
					and
					<a
						href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}books/shop-before-life`}
						class="text-blue-500 underline hover:text-blue-400"
						>The Shop Before Life</a
					>, for <strong class="text-red-500">free</strong>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="mb-6 px-12">
		<Quote
			quote={[
				'Your emails make me howl. With laughter, I hasten to add!',
				'I think they could be sold to a major publisher. Thank you for entertaining me.',
			]}
			cite={{ name: 'A long-time subscriber' }}
		/>
	</div>

	<div class="group flex justify-center px-3 pt-6 pb-7">
		<LinkButton
			className="px-5 pt-4 pb-5 font-serif text-2xl"
			url="http://eepurl.com/gB3e8P"
			text="Click here to sign up!"
		/>
	</div>

	<div class="space-y-3 bg-violet-100 px-12 py-3 md:space-y-6">
		<ul class="space-y-3 px-12">
			<li>
				👉 You can expect to receive an email newsletter from me ‘occasionally’;
				in practice, this means roughly every few weeks to every few months.
			</li>
			<li>
				✍️ The content of these emails can be quite varied, but they tend to be
				mainly humorous or thought-provoking stories, along with roundups of
				links to interesting things I've found, and articles I've written
				recently.
			</li>
			<li>
				❗ I don't store any of your data myself: at the time of writing I am
				using <a
					href="http://mailchimp.com"
					class="text-blue-500 underline hover:text-blue-400"
				>
					Mailchimp</a
				> to manage my email list, which means they will store the data you provide
				on my behalf.
			</li>
			<li>
				🥳 Naturally, <strong> you can unsubscribe at any time</strong>—an
				unsubscribe link is provided in every email.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</div>
